omments/6064666579/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6078791996","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124279#issuecomment-6078791996","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124279","id":6078791996,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABalMBPA","user":{"login":"PabloDevGit","id":19652075,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NjUyMDc1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19652075?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit","html_url":"https://github.com/PabloDevGit","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PabloDevGit/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-09T10:08:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T10:36:25Z","body":"Could we cache the invalid cells in _draw_overlay() and only invoke get_used_cells() when a modification event is triggered on the TileMapLayer (or when changing layers/TileSet), instead of querying it every frame? I tested this approach with the help of AI, and editor performance during pan/zoom improved by around 50-60%.\n\nEdit:\nJust to add a bit more context to my previous comment — please take this as exploratory feedback/brainstorming. I'm a developer, but I don't work with C++ or Godot's internal C++ codebase, so I've been experimenting with these ideas using AI assistance.\n\nTo actually achieve a noticeable performance improvement during pan/zoom, the caching needs to cover two main areas:\n\nAvoid calling get_used_cells() every frame inside _draw_overlay(), invoking it only when a change is detected on the TileMapLayer (e.g. tile placed/removed, or changing active layer/TileSet).\n\nCache the generated warning colors (hash/RandomPCG/HSV conversions) alongside the invalid cell coordinates during that same update event. Recalculating the array hash and random color per invalid cell on every single render frame turned out to be a major part of the performance hit as well.\n\nWhile no changes occur on the TileMap, neither get_used_cells() nor the random color generation should run inside the frame overlay loop._","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6078791996/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6078841365","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/124279#issuecomment-6078841365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124279","id":6078841365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABalPCFQ","user":{"login":"Flaybe","id":8083756,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwODM3NTY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8083756?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flaybe","html_url":"https://github.com/Flaybe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flaybe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flaybe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flaybe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flaybe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_ur